# Finora web — environment template.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in real values for local development. `.env` is
# gitignored; never commit real secrets. Only this placeholder file is tracked.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database (local development uses Docker Postgres; see README).
# `DATABASE_URL` is used by both the app and drizzle-kit migrations.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
POSTGRES_USER=finora
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=change-me-local-dev-only
POSTGRES_DB=finora
DATABASE_URL=postgres://finora:change-me-local-dev-only@127.0.0.1:15432/finora

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Session signing secret (HMAC key for the JWT session cookie).
# Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SESSION_SECRET=change-me-at-least-32-bytes-of-random-data

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: public origin used to build absolute links in recovery emails
# (scheme + host, optional port, no trailing path). Defaults to the local
# dev server origin when unset.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# APP_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Email delivery (email verification + password recovery) via Resend
# (https://resend.com). Read ONLY by server-side code
# (src/lib/email/adapter.ts) — never expose them through NEXT_PUBLIC_*.
#
# Default local development (values in this `.env` file):
#   Messages are logged to the console. Set EMAIL_OUTBOX_DIR to write them as
#   JSON files to a local directory instead (gitignored; never an HTTP
#   endpoint). Development NEVER sends real email by default, even when the
#   Resend variables below are set.
#
# Manual local delivery testing (explicit opt-in):
#   Put the two Resend variables plus the flag in a SEPARATE
#   `apps/web/.env.development.local` file (gitignored; loaded ONLY by
#   `next dev` — never by `next start`, the E2E suite or unit tests):
#     RESEND_API_KEY=re_replace_me
#     EMAIL_FROM="Finora <no-reply@example.com>"
#     EMAIL_PROVIDER=resend
#   The flag is read only outside production; an unknown value, or a partial
#   Resend configuration, falls back to the console/outbox behaviour above.
#
# Automated tests vs manual testing:
#   Unit tests mock the provider and never call Resend. The Playwright E2E
#   suite forces RESEND_API_KEY, EMAIL_FROM and EMAIL_PROVIDER to empty
#   strings for the server it spawns, so it can never send real email — stop
#   any server already running on port 3000 first, because a reused process
#   keeps its own environment. Manual local testing is the ONLY way real
#   email leaves this machine.
#
# Production (NODE_ENV=production):
#   - BOTH RESEND_API_KEY and EMAIL_FROM set  -> messages are sent through
#     Resend. That is the only production adapter (EMAIL_PROVIDER is ignored
#     in production — selection depends on configuration alone).
#   - Either one missing                     -> every send fails closed with
#     the same generic, enumeration-safe "service unavailable" answer. There
#     is NO console/file-outbox fallback in production, and the server logs a
#     startup warning naming the missing variables.
#
# RESEND_API_KEY  Server-only API key from the Resend dashboard (re_...).
#                 Keep it out of client code and NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables.
# EMAIL_FROM      Verified sender, e.g. "Finora <no-reply@example.com>".
#                 The sending domain must be verified in Resend (add the DNS
#                 records Resend shows) — a valid API key alone does NOT
#                 deliver mail. Account restrictions on Resend's free tier:
#                 the built-in "onboarding@resend.dev" test sender only
#                 delivers to your own account address, and sends from your
#                 own domain require the domain verification above.
# EMAIL_PROVIDER  Development-only opt-in. `resend` selects the real provider
#                 in `next dev` when BOTH variables above are set; any other
#                 value (or none) keeps the console/outbox default. Ignored
#                 in production and neutralised in the E2E suite.
#
# Configuration is required but not sufficient: the key must be valid and the
# sender/domain verified, or individual sends fail at request time with the
# same generic answer. Configuration never guarantees delivery — confirm
# actual status in the Resend dashboard. Never put real credentials in this
# file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EMAIL_OUTBOX_DIR=.email-outbox
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_replace_me
# EMAIL_FROM="Finora <no-reply@example.com>"
# EMAIL_PROVIDER=resend
